  "schema:name": "Interoperability Middleware",
  "schema:description": "A specialized software layer that connects disparate, otherwise incompatible computer applications, databases, and devices. It extracts data from a source system, translates it into a standardized format, and routes it to a destination system without requiring the core architecture of either system to be modified&#xD;\n&#xD;\nExample: Ensuring all applications used are intergrated with one another, having a centralized database&#xD;",
